From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 16:38:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/86] web-app: suppress the native context menu where the app
 owns one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two right-click targets opened the browser's own context menu on top of
the app's. Both are the same mistake — the handler that opens an app menu
does not cancel the native one in time — and both only bite the web
build, because Electron's menu template comes out empty in these spots
(no selection, not editable, no link) and so nothing is drawn.

- Chat list (`useChatContextMenu`): the handler awaits `getFullChatById`
  before reaching `openContextMenuInternalHandler`'s `preventDefault`,
  which is far too late; the browser has already taken the default action
  by the time the promise resolves. Cancel synchronously, up front.
- Webxdc app icon in the chat header (`AppIcon`): the handler never
  called `preventDefault` at all. Only the inner <img> guarded itself, so
  a right-click anywhere else on the button — its padding — got both
  menus. Cancel in the handler that owns the menu and drop the now
  redundant <img> guard, so one place decides.

Deliberately NOT a blanket suppressor: the native menu is the useful one
wherever the app has no menu of its own — selected text (the group name
in a profile is `user-select: text` precisely so it can be copied),
editable fields, images and links. Electron shows exactly those four, so
matching it means suppressing per-site, not globally.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/ChatView.tsx    | 7 ++++++-
 packages/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatContextMenu.tsx | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/ChatView.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/ChatView.tsx
index 19fbda5..85f2b38 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/ChatView.tsx
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/ChatView/ChatView.tsx
@@ -389,6 +389,12 @@ function AppIcon({ accountId, app }: { accountId: number; app: T.Message }) {
         )
       }}
       onContextMenu={event => {
+        // Before anything else: this element owns a context menu, so the
+        // native one must not also open on top of it. (Electron shows nothing
+        // here unless the pointer is over the icon image, so upstream only
+        // guarded the <img>; a browser shows its own menu for the whole
+        // button.)
+        event.preventDefault()
         openContextMenu({
           ...mouseEventToPosition(event),
           items: [
@@ -415,7 +421,6 @@ function AppIcon({ accountId, app }: { accountId: number; app: T.Message }) {
         className={styles.webxdcIcon}
         src={runtime.getWebxdcIconURL(accountId, app.id)}
         alt={appName}
-        onContextMenu={(e: React.MouseEvent) => e.preventDefault()}
       />
     </Button>
   )
diff --git a/packages/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatContextMenu.tsx b/packages/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatContextMenu.tsx
index 60d6f43..5a93f1c 100644
--- a/packages/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatContextMenu.tsx
+++ b/packages/frontend/src/components/chat/ChatContextMenu.tsx
@@ -326,6 +326,14 @@ export function useChatContextMenu(): {
     chatListItems: ChatListItem[],
     activeChatId: number | null
   ) => {
+    // Suppress the browser's native context menu synchronously, before the
+    // `await` below. `openContextMenuInternalHandler` also calls
+    // `preventDefault`, but that runs after this async function yields on the
+    // `getFullChatById` await, which is too late for the browser: the default
+    // action has already been taken and the native menu shows on top of ours.
+    // (On desktop Electron there is no native context menu, so this only bites
+    // the web build.)
+    event.preventDefault()
     // only if chatListItems contains a single chat, we need the full chat
     const selectedChat =
       chatListItems.length === 1
